Mind Map Architect (mmarchitect) Installation
---------------------------------------------

To build and install Mind Map Architect you need Meson, a Vala compiler,
gettext and the libraries listed in CONTRIBUTING.md:

    $ meson setup build
    $ meson compile -C build
    $ meson test -C build
    $ sudo meson install -C build
    $ sudo update-mime-database /usr/local/share/mime

By default mmarchitect is installed under the /usr/local directory. Use the
standard Meson options to change it, for example:

    $ meson setup build --prefix=/usr

To run the program from the build directory without installing it:

    $ DATADIR=. ./build/src/mmarchitect

To uninstall it, run in the build directory:

    $ sudo ninja uninstall

Windows
-------

The program is built with MSYS2 (https://www.msys2.org/). In the UCRT64
shell (or CLANGARM64 on ARM) install the tools and libraries:

    $ pacman -S --needed mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-toolchain \
        mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-meson mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-vala \
        mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-pkgconf mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gettext-tools \
        mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gtk3 mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-libgee \
        mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-librsvg mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-libxml2

and build it like on Linux:

    $ meson setup build --buildtype=release
    $ meson compile -C build
    $ meson test -C build

The CI runs exactly these steps, see .github/workflows/build.yml.

